    "method:rack::dsp::ComplexFFT::scale(float *)": {
      "finding": "P1: unjustified, undocumented restriction: the binding raises ValueError when the writable length field is negative (native/bindings/dsp/advanced.cpp:215), but Rack's ComplexFFT::scale (include/dsp/fft.hpp: `float a = 1.f / length; for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) ...`) is then a well-defined no-op, so Rack would not crash, assert or hit UB; docs/reference/dsp.md#dsp-fft and the record notes do not mention the refusal. Smallest fix: for length <= 0 check the buffer against 0 floats and call Rack's scale (a no-op), or document the refusal in dsp-fft and the notes.",
      "verdict": "finding"
    },
